    "summary": "Merriam-Webster defines a sandwich as 'two or more slices of bread or a split roll having a filling in between' and has stated that a hot dog is a sandwich. In 2015 the National Hot Dog and Sausage Council declared that a hot dog is not a sandwich; competitive eaters Joey Chestnut and Takeru Kobayashi agree with the council. On The Late Show in 2018, Justice Ruth Bader Ginsburg said a hot dog might be categorized as a sandwich, but that it comes down to the definition.",
